Publish, transmit, distribute, mirror, republish, sublicense, sell, lease, or otherwise make copies of the Software available outside rights necessarily exercised through the authorised Repository-hosting platform.

### 5.5 Competitive replication

Use substantial protectable portions of the Software, its implementation, or its original project materials to create or operate a substantially derived competing or substitute service.

Nothing in this paragraph restricts independent development that does not infringe copyright or other applicable rights.

### 5.6 Removal of notices

Remove, conceal, falsify, or materially alter copyright, licence, provenance, trademark, or ownership notices.

### 5.7 Circumvention

Circumvent technological or contractual restrictions imposed to protect the Software or gain access to non-public portions of the Software without authorisation.

### 5.8 Assistance

Knowingly enable, procure, direct, or materially assist another person to perform an act prohibited by this Licence.

