Except under a Separate Licence Agreement or to the extent mandatory law prevents restriction, the Software may not be systematically collected, scraped, ingested, reproduced, or processed for the principal purpose of:

- training an artificial-intelligence or machine-learning model;
- fine-tuning model weights;
- creating training, validation, evaluation, or benchmark datasets;
- improving code-generation models through model training;
- creating embeddings or derived datasets intended for model training or commercial model development;
- reconstructing or learning substantial implementation details for automated reproduction of the Software; or
- creating an automated system primarily intended to replicate substantial protectable portions of the Software.

This Section does not by itself prohibit a person from using ordinary development or accessibility tools merely to inspect small portions of the Software for a permitted Evaluation purpose, provided such use does not create or contribute to a training dataset, model, competing implementation, or prohibited derivative exploitation.

Rights separately granted to a Repository-hosting provider under that provider’s governing terms are unaffected to the extent the Copyright Holder has validly granted those rights.

